assembly/assembly.md:79:Not used: the record cap CAP2 and its opening (removed, `design/architecture.md:543`); the wall microphone slots (removed, `design/architecture.md:654`); the reverse-mount light (replaced, `design/architecture.md:688`).
assembly/assembly.md:97:- **Join:** every board part of `design/bom.csv` to the under face of PCB1, with solder paste and one reflow. The parts: U1 (`main_chip`), U2 (`power_chip`, nPM1304, `design/architecture.md:563`), R71, R72, U3 (`storage`), U10, U4 (`screen_supply_chip`), U5 (`mic_1`) and U6 (`mic_2`), Knowles SPK0641HT4H-1 (`design/architecture.md:651`, `design/bom.csv:9`), J1 (`screen_connector`), ANT1 (`antenna`), L2, L3, L4, C3, C12, X1 (`crystal_32M`), X2 (`crystal_32k`), L1, FB1, R1, R2, C1, C2, C5, C4, C6, C7, C10, C14, C11, L10 (`screen_supply_coil`), C21, C26, C27, C24, C25, C23, C22, C28, C29, C31, C32, C35, C36, R31, R32, R57, R58, R60, C60, U11 (`motor_regulator`, TLV75530PDQNR, at X 0.0, Y 4.2), C83 (`motor_cap_in`, X 0.0, Y 5.45), C84 (`motor_cap_out`, X 1.2, Y 5.0) (`design/architecture.md:702`, `design/mech/thin/placement.csv:19` to `design/mech/thin/placement.csv:21`; the places are the model's proposal until the board layout confirms them, `design/architecture.md:757`), LED1 (`recording_led`, top-view KPG-1005SURC-TT on the under face at X -9.70, Y -2.10, `design/architecture.md:688`), R41 (820 ohm, `design/architecture.md:690`, `design/bom.csv:48`), Q2, U9, R61 and R62 (now on U11's enable pin, `design/architecture.md:702`), R66, R63, R64, R65, C61, C72, C80, C81, C82, C71, C73, C74, C75, C78, C79, C76, C77, C85, C86, C87, C88 (`design/bom.csv:72` to `design/bom.csv:74`), L71 (`power_coil_1`), L72 (`power_coil_2`). The motor switch and the motor diode of earlier versions are not fitted: they left the design (`design/architecture.md:702`). The test pads TP1 to TP22 (TP1, TP2, TP3, TP4, TP5, TP6, TP7, TP8, TP9, TP10, TP11, TP12, TP13, TP14, TP15, TP16, TP17, TP18, TP19, TP20, TP21, TP22) and the ribbon lands J_BAND_A and J_BAND_B are copper on the same face and get no paste [PROPOSED: reason, a solder bump on a test pad or a hot-bar land spoils the spring-pin contact and the hot-bar joint of step 16]. C13 is not mounted (`design/bom.csv:18`).
assembly/assembly.md:162:- **Locate:** the body drawing per size. The body file today is the outer shape only (`design/mfg/specs/body.md:5`); the cavities come from the inside model v6, one set per size (`design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:272`).
assembly/assembly.md:163:- **Before:** the body has, per the model v6 (`design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:275` to `design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:282`): the two floor slots 2.0 x 0.6 from X -3.5 to X -1.5, Y -5.9 and +5.9 (model v6.2, architecture 17.27; before it 2.6 x 0.6) (`design/mfg/specs/body.md:90`), with their bottom at the Z of the size (table above); the joystick opening 6.6 along the finger x 5.6 round the band at the joystick angle of the size, on the joystick side; the joystick pocket 7.0 along the finger x 6.8 round the band, open from the bore up to a flat roof at the radius of the size, with the channel left uncut over the joystick (`design/architecture.md:790`, `design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:249`); the glass seat lowered 0.05 mm under the glass footprint, outside the panel pocket (`design/mfg/specs/body.md:83`); the two floor pockets, 1.0 mm holes and 2.0 x 0.10 mm membrane seats at X -11.77 and +11.77, Y -4.8 (`design/architecture.md:654`, `design/mech/mic-path/mic-path.md:71` to `design/mech/mic-path/mic-path.md:73`); no wall slots and no pad holes (`design/architecture.md:554`); the motor pocket 5.2 x 2.6 at the motor angle of the size (`design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:273`).
assembly/assembly.md:235:- **Locate:** the slot 2.0 x 0.6 mm (model v6.2, `design/architecture.md` 17.27; before it 2.6 x 0.6) and the ribbon 1.4 x 0.15 in it: the open area to fill is 0.99 square mm per slot [CALC: 2.0 x 0.6 - 1.4 x 0.15; slot size `design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:21`]. The slot's bottom lies deeper on larger sizes (Z -0.20 on US 7 to Z -1.85 on US 13, table above), so the length of slot to fill changes by size.
assembly/assembly.md:286:- **Check:** every factory test again (`design/firmware.md:875` to `design/firmware.md:884`): T-RADIO now in the final body with glass (Bluetooth); USB enumeration proves the four pads; T-JOY and T-CENTRE (joystick); T-MOTOR (motor); T-MIC1 and T-MIC2 through the membranes (microphones); T-LIGHT through the print window (light); T-SCREEN through the glass (screen); T-STORE, T-XTAL, T-CHARGE. Then one test on the cell alone [PROPOSED]: VBUS off, a long press of the nub starts a recording with motor pulse M1, a second long press stops it; VBUS on again and GET_INFO shows the same boot count (`design/firmware.md:642`). Reason: the motor now runs from its own regulator U11 on the cell, outside the power chip's 100 mA battery limit, so a motor start no longer passes the power chip (`design/architecture.md:701`, `design/architecture.md:703`); but nothing is measured, and a start still takes up to 228 mA from the cell, whose own discharge limit and protection trip current are unknown (`design/architecture.md:707`, S12). This test shows on the real cell that the protection circuit does not trip and the ring does not reset; the jig's VBUS would hide it.
assembly/assembly.md:294:- **Check:** T-CHARGE shows the charger on; the battery voltage in the status record (`design/firmware.md:684`) rises. Charge to 50 percent before ship mode [PROPOSED: reason, a partly charged cell ages less in storage and still wakes the ring in the case; the cell maker may set another level, S12]. A full charge takes 1.17 to 2.13 hours over US 7 to 13 [CALC: 17.6 / 15 and 31.9 / 15; capacities `design/architecture.md:779`, `design/architecture.md:785`].
assembly/assembly.md:310:- **Check:** serial number, ring size and the test records of steps 5, 18, 21, 25 and 27 are kept together.
assembly/assembly.md:324:| K-A6 | Each ribbon has parts at its band end and a joint of 8 lands (FLEX1) or 7 lands (FLEX2) at its board end, and passes a closed slot of 2.0 x 0.6 mm (2.6 x 0.6 before model v6.2). So the board-end joint must be made after threading, with the board held above the block (step 16). The ribbon's slack needs room when the board goes down. | `design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:69`, `design/bom.csv:81`, `design/bom.csv:82`, `design/mfg/specs/band-flex-tails.md:61` | PROPOSAL: reserve a free area beside each slot on the under face for one fold of the ribbon. | CHANGED: the model v5 keeps a free volume of 2.6 x 2.2 x 1.03 mm beside each slot, checked empty (`design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:134`). Open: whether one fold fits that height (bend radius, K21, `design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:159`), and the board layout keeping it free (S14). |
assembly/assembly.md:328:| K-A10 | The body spec put the floor slots at X -4.7, outside the channel; the model needs X -2.2. | `design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:91` | PROPOSAL: change the body spec to X -2.2. | CLOSED: the body spec now says X -2.2 (`design/mfg/specs/body.md:90`); the model keeps it (`design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:117`). |
